{:edb/db-before-t 786 :edb/db-after-t 787 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534099 50 #inst "2026-10-06T02:52:27.036Z" 13194139534099 true] [17592186087828 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277547 13194139534099 true] [17592186087828 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277560 13194139534099 true] [17592186087829 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277550 13194139534099 true] [17592186087829 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277553 13194139534099 true] [17592186088034 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534099 true] [17592186088034 1100 "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t) = 2t^{3} - 3t^{2} + 2t$, where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the particle's acceleration at $t = 2$ seconds." 13194139534099 false] [17592186088034 1100 "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=2{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+2t$, where $t$ is measured in seconds.  Find the particle's acceleration at $t=2$ seconds." 13194139534099 true] [17592186088034 1145 "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+2t) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}-6t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}-6t+2) \\\\  & =12t-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=2$, we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =12(2)-6 \\\\  & =24-6 \\\\  & =18\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=2$ seconds is $18\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" 13194139534099 true] [17592186277547 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277548 13194139534099 true] [17592186277547 1089 "q-336423" 13194139534099 true] [17592186277547 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534099 true] [17592186277547 1100 "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=2{t}^{4}-3{t}^{2}+t,$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Calculate the acceleration of the particle at $t=1$ second.\n\n$a(1)=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" 13194139534099 true] [17592186277547 1113 #uuid "87f98f5f-15df-53f7-978f-c2984e68b9a9" 13194139534099 true] [17592186277547 1145 "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{4}-3{t}^{2}+t) \\\\  & =8{t}^{3}-6t+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration when $t=1$ second, we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =8(1)^{3}-6(1)+1 \\\\  & =8-6+1 \\\\  & =3\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534099 true] [17592186277548 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277549 13194139534099 true] [17592186277548 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534099 true] [17592186277548 1041 "field-1" 13194139534099 true] [17592186277548 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277549 13194139534099 true] [17592186277548 1110 #uuid "e8350234-5877-51a6-9b51-e83ed572de17" 13194139534099 true] [17592186277549 1034 "3" 13194139534099 true] [17592186277549 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534099 true] [17592186277549 1111 #uuid "9a1e7756-6302-5083-b4d2-426d7cc4ec74" 13194139534099 true] [17592186277550 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277551 13194139534099 true] [17592186277550 1089 "q-336452" 13194139534099 true] [17592186277550 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534099 true] [17592186277550 1100 "The displacement $s$ of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=5+3{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}.$ Find the particle's acceleration at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534099 true] [17592186277550 1113 #uuid "4a3a2898-11c1-5cbc-bf20-323ffecc5307" 13194139534099 true] [17592186277550 1145 "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5+3{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =6t-{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t